        "notes": "By this point you pretty much have the core of the build so you can choose which ever path fits your playstyle for Round 7.\n\n [Stinger](item_e9d0d530-d620-4e74-a34d-38cdebfeb9a4) and  [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) is one of my favourite combos.  [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) is just  [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) with a deadly debuff and  [Stinger](item_e9d0d530-d620-4e74-a34d-38cdebfeb9a4) will benefit from all the  [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) we've picked up. The combo is great because Juno can endlessly apply the debuff with Mediblaster.\n\nYou could continue the Hyper Ring theme with  [Black Hole](item_d9edbd0b-d1e2-4103-b8d4-6e1dc8124894) and make the ring extra nasty for the enemy. With all the  [Cooldown Reduction](stat_cooldown_reduction) we can fire it out very often so you'll get a lot out of this. Plus it really helps team mates who are retreating from dive heroes.\n\n [Medicinal Missiles](item_30eeab6c-4a1e-4a16-b9dd-e83d633caa40) might also be handy in the final round if your team has been struggling for heals, or you just want to over heal with Mercy. You can bring this in for round 5 if you prefer instead of  [Rally Ring](item_0547012b-4817-437e-aad3-aa37db93383e) \n\nGenerally for the abilities you can look at simply increasing your power with [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6)  or [Champion's Kit](item_8682f8c7-8811-439b-8d50-fa81cd43ddce), doing the  [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) combo mentioned above, or going for other favourites like  [Pulsar Destroyers](item_707ad8c7-a153-4140-b4bc-1f23f7d7a648)",
